@startuml
title SIC/XE Simulator - Source Load with the Macro Processor
autonumber
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Frontend client" as Client
participant "Server /ws handler" as Server
participant "Simulator" as Sim
participant "SICXE::load_file" as Arch
participant "sicxe::MacroProcessor" as Macro
participant "macroReportJson /\nMacrosExpanded event" as Report
participant "sicxe::Assembler" as Asm
participant "MemoryAccessor /\nRegisterAccessor (loader)" as Loader

Client -> Server : {id, type: "command",\npayload: "load %file-path"}
Server -> Sim : event_count() as eventStart
Server -> Sim : load_file(path)
Sim -> Arch : load_file(file text)
Arch -> Arch : clear(): MemoryCleared,\nregister writes, ProgramCleared

alt text starts with ';' (hexadecimal dump)
  Arch -> Loader : write the dump at address 0, PC = 0
  note right of Arch
  The macro processor does not run.
  end note
else assembly source
  Arch -> Macro : process(content)
  Macro --> Arch : MacroResult macros
  Arch -> Report : macroReportJson(macros)
  Report --> Arch : details
  Arch -> Report : execute(MacrosExpanded(details))\nbefore assembling
  alt !macros.ok()
    Arch --> Sim : throw runtime_error(\nformatDiagnostics(macros.diagnostics))
  else processor ok
    Arch -> Asm : assembleDetailed(macros.text)
    Asm --> Arch : AssemblyResult assembled
    alt !assembled.ok()
      Arch --> Sim : throw runtime_error(formatDiagnostics(\nremapAssemblyDiagnostics(macros, content, ...)))
    else assembled
      Arch -> Loader : write(0, assembled.memory)\nPC = entryPoint
      Arch -> Arch : ProgramAssembled(symbols)
    end
  end
end

alt load threw
  Sim --> Server : exception
  Server -> Sim : event_batch(eventStart)
  Sim --> Server : events so far, MacrosExpanded included
  Server --> Client : {id, error: {type, status, title,\ndetail "L:C: error: msg", events}}
else load succeeded
  Arch -> Arch : InstructionFetched preview at PC
  Arch --> Sim : events
  Sim --> Server : EventBatch {from, to, events}
  Server --> Client : {id, result: {from, to, events}}
end

note over Arch,Asm
The assembler assembles MASMAPRG.ASM (macros.text).
A source without macros comes out of the processor
byte for byte, so it assembles as before.
source_line in InstructionFetched is a MASMAPRG.ASM line.
end note
@enduml
